no Accept header  ->  1.0 1.0 1.0
application/json  ->  application/json=1.0  text/plain=0.0  text/csv=0.0
application/json;q=0.5, text/plain  ->  application/json=0.5  text/plain=1.0  text/csv=0.0
text/*;q=0.8  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=0.8  text/csv=0.8
*/*;q=0.3  ->  application/json=0.3  text/plain=0.3  text/csv=0.3
*/*, text/*;q=0  ->  application/json=1.0  text/plain=0.0  text/csv=0.0
*/*;q=0.1, text/plain;q=0.9  ->  application/json=0.1  text/plain=0.9  text/csv=0.1
text/*;q=0.2, text/csv  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=0.2  text/csv=1.0
application/json;q=0, */*  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=1.0  text/csv=1.0
text/*;q=0.2, text/*;q=0.9  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=0.9  text/csv=0.9
text/plain;q=high  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=1.0  text/csv=0.0
text/plain;q=  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=1.0  text/csv=0.0
text/plain;q=5, text/csv  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=5.0  text/csv=1.0
text/plain;q=-1, text/csv;q=0.1  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=-1.0  text/csv=0.1
not a media type, text/plain;q=0.4  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=0.4  text/csv=0.0
  ->  application/json=0.0  text/plain=0.0  text/csv=0.0

prefers csv            -> text/csv
prefers plain          -> text/plain
no preference          -> text/plain
no preference, csv 1st -> text/csv
wildcard only          -> text/plain
refuses both           -> none acceptable
refuses one            -> text/csv
wants what is not here -> none acceptable
no candidates          -> none acceptable

accepts json, weighted    -> true
accepts json, zero exact  -> false
accepts json, zero spelt  -> false
accepts json, no header   -> true
accepts json, wildcard    -> true
